{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122025","id":4188140895,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc75ofVf","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122025","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122025.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122025.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122025","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122025/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122025/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122025/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e31789449c7f76247dab36ee9c4e2567534f2d3b","number":122025,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[Docs] Add a note how to use EditorPaths class","user":{"login":"Overkane","id":29690395,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjkwMzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29690395?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane","html_url":"https://github.com/Overkane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Overkane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nExplains the intended way to use EditorPaths class.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nMy use case:\r\n- I wanted to use EditorPaths singleton for my plugin to get settings directory.\r\n- Docs say it is a singleton. Ok, I tried to use it as `EditorPaths.get_config_dir()`.\r\n- Didn't work, godot said I need to instantiate it first. Ok, I tried to instantiate it first  with `EditotorPaths.new()` and then call the method. I got error \"Condition \"singleton != nullptr\" is true\" which is not really descriptive and at this point I'm stuck and thinking it is some kind of engine bug.\r\n- I tried to ask AI, and with second attempt (first one was about using `EditorPaths.get_config_dir()` directly too) it tells me that there is actually a `EditorInterface.get_config_dir()` method. I usually use F1 in editor, so I didn't know there was a function which returns this singleton.\r\n\r\nSo in this PR I added a note, similar to the one used in e.g. EditorToaster or EditorSettings classes, which tells how you are supposed to access this singleton.\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg4Mzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"","color":"ffddff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"h